      "message": "1. \n```\n25-10-08 12:18:59.164C1: RECV 05b6/0\n25-10-08 12:18:59.425[54.711500 tx_status \u003d 0\n25-10-08 12:18:59.428 ]\n25-10-08 12:18:59.428[54.712400 tx_status \u003d 0\n25-10-08 12:18:59.430 ]\n25-10-08 12:18:59.430[54.714000 tx1 \u003d 1, tx2 \u003d 1\n25-10-08 12:18:59.436 ]\n25-10-08 12:18:59.436[54.713900 tx_status \u003d 0\n25-10-08 12:18:59.438 ]\n25-10-08 12:18:59.438[54.717800 xmit_status \u003d 1\n25-10-08 12:18:59.441 ]\n25-10-08 12:18:59.441C1: RECV 97a4/1[0]00088001\n25-10-08 12:18:59.449[54.726200 tx_status \u003d 0\n25-10-08 12:18:59.452 ]\n25-10-08 12:18:59.452[54.728400 tx1 \u003d 1, tx2 \u003d 1\n25-10-08 12:18:59.455 ]\n25-10-08 12:18:59.455[54.729000 xmit_status \u003d 1\n25-10-08 12:18:59.458 ]\n```\nHere, `RECV 05b6/0` is the `Get_Sink_Caps_Extended` and `RECV 97a4/1[0]00088001` is the `Get Battery Status`.\n\n2. Will do the same on `port1` with the local variable change. What would be the best way to do it on `port0`?",
